<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 135 0 R/T(Question as given: Write a program to implement the C-SCAN and LOOK disk scheduling algorithms. The program should accept inputs including the request queue, the initial head position, and the direction of head movement \(left or right\). It must simulate both algorithms, calculate the total head movement required to service all requests, and compare their efficiency. The output should display the seek sequence, total head movement, and a conclusion indicating which algorithm performs better along with a brief justification. Optionally, the program may include a graphical visualization of head movement.)/E(Question as given: Write a program to implement the C-SCAN and LOOK disk scheduling algorithms. The program should accept inputs including the request queue, the initial head position, and the direction of head movement \(left or right\). It must simulate both algorithms, calculate the total head movement required to service all requests, and compare their efficiency. The output should display the seek sequence, total head movement, and a conclusion indicating which algorithm performs better along with a brief justification. Optionally, the program may include a graphical visualization of head movement.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[4]>>
