<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 140 0 R/T(What This Question Is Asking)/E(What This Question Is Asking)/Pg 30 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

1087 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 140 0 R/T(\200 Try Contiguous allocation on one copy of the disk map, and Indexed allocation on a separate copy of the disk map, so one method's success/failure never affects the other.)/E(\200 Try Contiguous allocation on one copy of the disk map, and Indexed allocation on a separate copy of the disk map, so one method's success/failure never affects the other.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

1088 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 140 0 R/T(\200 For each allocation method that succeeds, merge its allocated block numbers)/E(\200 For each allocation method that succeeds, merge its allocated block numbers)/Pg 30 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

1089 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 140 0 R/T(with the externally pending disk requests, removing duplicates, to build the disk- scheduling request queue.)/E(with the externally pending disk requests, removing duplicates, to build the disk- scheduling request queue.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1090 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 140 0 R/T(\200 This is a combined question: first a file must actually be allocated space on the disk \(using Contiguous or Indexed allocation\), and then the disk arm must be scheduled to visit the blocks that were allocated \(using FCFS or SSTF\), together with any other pending disk requests.)/E(\200 This is a combined question: first a file must actually be allocated space on the disk \(using Contiguous or Indexed allocation\), and then the disk arm must be scheduled to visit the blocks that were allocated \(using FCFS or SSTF\), together with any other pending disk requests.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[10]>>
