<</Title(Question as given: Write a program to simulate the three file allocation methods\204 Contiguous, Linked, and Indexed. The program should accept inputs including the total disk size \(number of blocks\), the file size \(number of blocks required\), and the allocation method \(1 for Contiguous, 2 for Linked, 3 for Indexed\). Based on the selected method, the program must allocate disk blocks accordingly, display the allocated block numbers, and handle fragmentation scenarios, particularly when contiguous allocation fails due to insufficient continuous space. The output should show the list of allocated blocks or an appropriate error message if allocation is not possible. Ensure that built-in memory allocation functions are not used, and assume that disk blocks are numbered starting from 0.)/Dest[10 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2160 0 R/Prev 2242 0 R/Next 2325 0 R>>
endobj

